@@ -0,0 +1,274 @@
+# Effect Authority & Path-Conflict Fix Spec
+
+Status: APPROVED FOR IMPLEMENTATION (2026-08-24)
+Author: main session (Fable). Investigations: two audit agents, findings personally
+verified line-by-line before inclusion — every claim below carries checked line numbers.
+
+User-reported symptoms this spec resolves:
+1. Mode switches revert on their own ("該切換了卻跑回另一個模式")
+2. Parameter edits don't take effect immediately, then change mid-run ("延遲/亂序生效")
+3. With a music-note bokeh mask, the soft halo around large emissive surfaces degrades
+   into coarse note fragments, then silently heals ("音符碎片…不知何時又好了")
+
+Root-cause summary (verified):
+- Symptoms 1+2 are genuine *write-path fights*: two ownership authorities that desync
+  (`s_pActive` vs `ICameraManager`), a RESET handler that runs the restore sweep on
+  BOTH directions of the mode toggle, per-frame cvar force-backs, and stale-baseline
+  save/restore across `ResetPostEffects()`.
+- Symptom 3 is NOT a fight: it is a sampling degeneracy in the mask-CDF gather kernel
+  (a 7×7 regular grid feeds CDF inversion → at most 7 distinct mask rows are ever
+  sampled; the 3×3 second pass hits only 3 rows). Domain flips (see A4/R2) merely make
+  it intermittent, which is why it looked timing-related.
+
+Division of labour:
+- Section A (component lifecycle, CinematicCameraComponent.cpp/.h + Plugin.cpp):
+  implementation agent.
+- Section R (renderer: gather kernel math, CParamTexture sync, domain logging):
+  main session personally — semantic/cross-system per working rule.
+
+Build: bundled CMake only (`Tools\CMake\Win32\bin\cmake.exe`). Targets:
+CinematicCamera (section A), CryRenderD3D11 (section R). Profile config, zero warnings.
+Never touch `CryRenderD3D11.dll.official-backup`.
+
+---
+
+## Section A — Component: single authority, correct mode transitions
+
+File: `Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/Module/CinematicCameraComponent.cpp/.h`,
+`CinematicCameraPlugin.cpp`. All line numbers are current-tree, verified.
+
+### A1. One ownership authority: the camera manager decides, `s_pActive` follows
+
+Today `s_pActive` (set only in Initialize/Activate/Deactivate/OnShutDown) and
+`ICameraManager`'s active camera (moves whenever ANY `CCameraComponent` activates)
+are independent and silently desync (verified: `Deactivate()` :266-286 never touches
+the sibling; `IsActive()` :288-291 delegates to the manager, so a "deactivated"
+component still owns the view; the plugin hook `CinematicCameraPlugin.cpp:30-37` keys
+off `s_pActive` and keeps stealing `SetViewCamera` after the manager moved on).
+
+Change — make the manager the single authority, `s_pActive` a derived cache:
+
+1. Maintain a static registry `static std::vector<CCinematicCameraComponent*> s_all;`
+   — push in `Initialize()`, erase in `OnShutDown()`. (Single-threaded main-thread
+   use only; no locking.)
+2. Add a static resolver, called ONCE per frame from the plugin hook before anything
+   else:
+   ```
+   CCinematicCameraComponent* CCinematicCameraComponent::ResolveActive()
+   {
+       CCinematicCameraComponent* pManagerActive = nullptr;
+       for (auto* p : s_all)
+           if (p->m_pCameraComponent && p->m_pCameraComponent->IsActive())
+               { pManagerActive = p; break; }
+       if (pManagerActive != s_pActive)
+       {
+           if (s_pActive)           // dethroned: give the render state back
+               s_pActive->RestoreAllEffects();
+           s_pActive = pManagerActive;
+           if (s_pActive)
+               s_pActive->m_pEntity->UpdateComponentEventMask(s_pActive);
+       }
+       return s_pActive;
+   }
+   ```
+   `RestoreAllEffects()` = the existing 7-Restore sweep + RestoreExposure-if-saved
+   (factor it out of `Deactivate()`; it appears verbatim in 3 places today:
+   :268-280, :243-250, :191-203).
+3. Plugin hook becomes:
+   ```
+   if (CCinematicCameraComponent* pActive = CCinematicCameraComponent::ResolveActive())
+   {
+       pActive->FinalizeGameCamera();
+       pActive->ApplyExposureGlobalParam();
+   }
+   ```
+   This fixes the "our camera can never be dethroned" bug: when a non-cinematic
+   `CCameraComponent` becomes manager-active, ResolveActive returns nullptr, we stop
+   finalizing, restore once, and the other camera's own Update owns the view.
+4. `Initialize()` :119-125 — DELETE the block (`s_pActive = this`, ApplyDOF). The
+   resolver picks the manager-active camera on the first frame; Initialize must not
+   claim ownership (verified today every cinematic camera claims it at construction
+   because the sibling auto-activates before :113 disables auto-activation — last
+   initialized wins arbitrarily).
+5. `Activate()` :240-253 — keep `m_pCameraComponent->Activate()` (that IS the
+   authority transfer); DELETE the manual old-active restore block :241-251 and
+   `s_pActive = this` :253 — the resolver handles both next frame. Keep
+   `UpdateComponentEventMask`. Change the trailing `ApplyDOF()` per A5.
+6. `Deactivate()` — semantic note (document in the header comment): the engine always
+   needs SOME active view; deactivating a cinematic camera cannot null the manager.
+   New meaning: "strip cinematic effects, remain a plain view until another camera
+   activates". Implementation: `RestoreAllEffects(); m_bCinematicSuspended = true;`
+   plus event-mask update. `ResolveActive()` must treat a suspended component as
+   not-active (skip in the loop); `Activate()` clears the flag before
+   `m_pCameraComponent->Activate()`.
+7. `IsActive()` stays manager-delegating but add the suspension:
+   `return !m_bCinematicSuspended && m_pCameraComponent && m_pCameraComponent->IsActive();`
+
+### A2. Ownership gate on EVERY push
+
+`ApplySpriteBokeh()` :796 already has `if (s_pActive != this) return;`. Hoist into a
+shared predicate and use it in ALL apply paths (verified `ApplyDOF()` :487 has no
+guard and is reached from the per-entity UPDATE event :156-157 — with two DOF-enabled
+cameras the f-numbers come from one camera and the shape texture from another, mixing
+two cameras into one domain decision):
+
+```
+bool CanDriveRenderState() const
+{
+    return s_pActive == this
+        && m_pEntity->GetSimulationMode() != EEntitySimulationMode::Preview;
+}
+```
+Early-return with it in: `ApplyDOF`, `ApplyLensCharacter`, `ApplyFilmGrain`,
+`ApplyMotionBlur`, `ApplyWhiteBalance`, `ApplyStreaks`, `ApplyExposureGlobalParam`.
+(`ApplySpriteBokeh` keeps its existing check; replacing it with the shared one is fine.)
+The PROPERTY_CHANGED handler :174-187 currently calls `ApplyLensCharacter()`
+unconditionally — verified this lets ANY selected cinematic camera (even a Preview-mode
+one) write the global vignette/distortion cvars and latch a baseline. The gate fixes it.
+
+### A3. RESET is bidirectional — branch on `nParam[0]`
+
+Verified: `EntitySystem.cpp:1489-1492` sends ENTITY_EVENT_RESET with `nParam[0]=1`
+entering simulation/game, `0` leaving; our handler :189-205 ignores it and runs the
+full restore sweep in BOTH directions. Entering game mode the sweep writes stale
+edit-mode-captured values over the state `ResetPostEffects()` (GameEngine.cpp:809)
+just cleared.
+
+```
+case ENTITY_EVENT_RESET:
+    if (event.nParam[0] == 0)
+    {
+        // Leaving game mode: give the render state back.
+        RestoreAllEffects();
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        // Entering game/simulation mode. ResetPostEffects() already wiped the
+        // renderer to defaults, so our edit-mode baselines are stale. Drop them
+        // WITHOUT writing: the next Apply* re-latches from the fresh defaults.
+        ClearSavedBaselines();
+    }
+    m_pEntity->UpdateComponentEventMask(this);
+    break;
+```
+`ClearSavedBaselines()` = set every `m_b*Saved` flag false (`m_bDofParamsSaved`,
+`m_bSpriteBokehSaved`, grain/mblur/WB/lens/streaks/exposure equivalents) WITHOUT any
+SetPostEffectParam/cvar writes. Also reset `m_bBokehShapeTexPushed = false`.
+
+### A4. Save/restore the three leaked DOF params
+
+Verified in `ApplyDOF()`/`RestoreDOF()` :487-549: `Dof_Active` is forced to 0 every
+frame (:510) and NEVER restored — after a cinematic camera has run once, the scene's
+own (TrackView/flowgraph) DOF is dead for the session. `Dof_User_ApertureBlades`
+(:515) and `Dof_User_FNumber` (:516) are pushed but not saved/restored either.
+Add all three to the save block (:496-508) and to `RestoreDOF()`.
+
+Note for the implementer: `Dof_Active` is ALSO written per-frame by TrackView
+(`AnimCameraNode.cpp:188/197`) and GameSDK camera code; last-writer-wins per frame is
+acceptable and out of scope — the fix here is only that WE restore what we saved.
+
+### A5. Edit-mode policy — uniform, not half-and-half
+
+Verified inconsistency: `ApplyDOF` runs from `Initialize` :124 and `Activate` :263
+with no `IsEditing()` guard, while UPDATE :156, PROPERTY_CHANGED :177 and the three
+setters skip it in edit mode. Result: a stale DOF push from load-time sits in the
+renderer, ignores every subsequent property edit, and snaps to real values only when
+game mode starts — this IS symptom 2's "調完沒生效、之後突然變".
+
+Decision (mine): policy (a) — view-dependent effects are game-mode only, because in
+edit mode the viewport renders through the editor fly camera and pushing the cinematic
+camera's focus/blur onto it produces meaningless imagery. View-independent character
+(vignette, distortion, exposure) stays live in the editor for authoring feedback,
+gated by A2.
+
+Concretely:
+- Remove `ApplyDOF()` from `Initialize()` (whole block goes per A1.4).
+- In `Activate()`: `if (!gEnv->IsEditing() && m_dof.bEnableDOF) ApplyDOF();`
+- UPDATE/PROPERTY_CHANGED/setters keep their `!IsEditing()` guards (unchanged).
+- `ApplyExposureGlobalParam` stays editor-live (existing behavior, users rely on it)
+  but now runs only for the resolver-confirmed active component (A1.3) — it already
+  did in practice; the change is that the resolver keeps `s_pActive` honest.
+- Vignette/distortion (`ApplyLensCharacter`) stays editor-live, gated by A2.
+
+Known consequence (accepted, tell the user): game-mode-only effects still cannot be
+tuned persistently from inside game mode — `EntityComponentsCache::RestoreEntities()`
+(EntitySystem.cpp:1476-1478) reverts property edits on exit. That is stock editor
+behavior for all components; not fought here.
+
+### A6. Regression checklist for the implementer
+
+After building CinematicCamera (bundled CMake, Profile, zero warnings), verify by
+code inspection and report:
+- exactly one call site sets `s_pActive` (the resolver);
+- every Apply* begins with the gate (A2);
+- RESET handler branches on nParam[0];
+- no Apply/Restore writes remain in the RESET-enter path;
+- `RestoreDOF` restores 12 params (9 existing + 3 from A4) + `r_dof`;
+- registry push/erase paired in Initialize/OnShutDown; OnShutDown still ends with the
+  old behavior (restore + clear) for the case where the destroyed component is active.
+DO NOT deploy DLLs; the main session deploys after review.
+
+---
+
+## Section R — Renderer (main session implements personally)
+
+File: `Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/DepthOfField.cpp`,
+`Common/PostProcess/PostProcess.cpp`.
+
+### R1. Mask-kernel sampling degeneracy (symptom 3 primary cause — verified :336-348,
+:382-394, :167-191)
+
+The 7×7 tap loop feeds a REGULAR grid (`t.y ∈ {0..6}/6`, only 7 distinct values) into
+`SampleMaskKernelTap`'s row-CDF inversion → all 49 taps land on at most 7 mask rows
+(3×3 pass: 3 rows). Thin vertical structure (note stem) becomes discrete horizontal
+bands; at large CoC each band is tens of pixels from the next → "coarse note
+fragments". The polygon path is immune (Shirley concentric mapping is area-preserving).
+
+Fix: for `bMaskKernel` only, replace the grid (u,v) with a deterministic
+low-discrepancy set — Hammersley: `u_i = (i + 0.5) / N`, `v_i = radicalInverse2(i)`
+(bit-reversal). N=49 first pass, N=9 second pass. Every tap then has a distinct v →
+CDF inversion can hit up to 49 distinct rows. Deterministic across frames (no temporal
+noise). `ToUnitDisk` path keeps the existing grid (its concentric mapping wants the
+stratified square).
+
+### R2. Silent domain flips / silent CDF fallback (symptom 3's "不知何時又好了" —
+verified :266-268 gather domain has no log; fallback result is cached per texture name)
+
+Add one-shot-on-change CryLog lines: (a) gather domain MASK↔iris transitions with the
+(N, maskN, texValid) triple; (b) `EnsureMaskKernelCDF` fallback-to-polygon including
+the reason string. No per-frame spam: log only when the value differs from the last
+logged state.
+
+### R3. `CParamTexture::SyncMainWithRender` no-op (verified PostProcess.cpp:779 —
+stock bug: assigns a local pointer where every other CParam type memcpys fill→process)
+
+Fix properly: copy the fill slot's texture binding into the process slot (with correct
+AddRef/Release pairing, matching what `Create()`/`Release()` do to a slot). This closes
+the one-frame skew where f-numbers (actively synced) and the shape texture (passively
+converged) come from different generations — the mask-domain flip window after any
+`CPostEffectsMgr::Reset` (quality change, `EF_ResetPostEffects`). The component's
+every-frame write stays (harmless, now redundant by design).
+
+### R4. User-path focus smoothing (symptom 2 contributor — verified
+PostProcessDOF.cpp:45-52, 82-99: two chained exponential smoothers + function-local
+statics that never reset, advanced per `GetParams()` call ON THE RENDER THREAD)
+
+Minimal, user-branch-only change: when `Dof_User_Active` is set (that path is
+effectively ours — the component drives its own focal motor and needs raw values),
+bypass the `m_fUser*Curr` smoothing and use the raw params directly. The
+TOD/non-user branch and its statics stay untouched. Flagged as a deliberate behavior
+change: focus edits become frame-exact instead of ~1/3s laggy.
+
+### R-deferred (documented, not in this round)
+
+- Splat coherent stacking (every splat is the same unrotated note; large emissive
+  areas stack them in phase). Re-evaluate after R1 — the gather fix may resolve the
+  visible complaint. Candidate later: per-splat sub-texel jitter of the quad UV.
+- Per-frame cvar force-back (`r_DepthOfFieldMode=0` :812-813, `r_dof=1` :493-494,
+  `r_MotionBlur=2`): intended property→cvar authority, but it stomps console
+  experiments. Deferred decision: possibly write only when OUR property changed.
+  Console users: toggle the component property instead of the cvar for now.
+- `m_pCameraComponent` dangling if the user deletes the sibling Camera component in
+  the editor UI (no removal hook). Low likelihood; revisit if it ever bites.
+- gather/splat domain divergence at `r_DepthOfFieldBokehQuality >= 3` is DELIBERATE
+  (diagnostic split), documented in code :263-265.
