@@ -0,0 +1,292 @@
+# CryPhoneTracker
+
+A native CRYENGINE 5.7 plugin providing the **Phone Tracker** entity component (Sandbox
+category: **Tracking / Phone Tracker**): it receives packets from the Android ARCore phone
+tracker (`cryengine-57-lts/androidtracker`), drives an entity's position and rotation from the
+6DoF pose, and forwards the lens faders on the phone (focal length / aperture / focus / ISO /
+EV) to a **Cinematic Camera** component.
+
+## Connection
+
+- The component opens a **UDP** socket when entering game/simulation mode (`Listen Port`,
+  default 9050), non-blocking, drained empty every frame, so the entity always follows the
+  newest pose instead of a backlog. In pure edit mode the entity receives no Update event and
+  does not move — that is engine behaviour.
+- In the phone app's Settings, enter the PC's LAN IP and the same port, transport UDP.
+- Control packets (Recenter, AF results) are sent back through the same socket to the address
+  the last packet came from.
+- **Port conflicts are named.** Two trackers on one port would silently fight over the bind
+  (and the loser would get no packets and no error), so before binding, the component looks
+  for another live tracker on the same port and refuses with
+  `PORT 9050 BUSY - held by tracker #2 'CamRig'` — shown both as a warning in the log and in
+  the debug overlay. A port taken outside the level reports
+  `PORT 9050 BIND FAILED - in use outside this level (another process?)`.
+
+### Tracker ID
+
+**Tracker ID** (Connection group, 0-99, default 0) is the number this tracker answers to in
+logs and in the debug overlay, so several trackers can be told apart. `0` means automatic:
+the tracker's position in creation order, 1-based. Every log line and the overlay carry it
+(`[PhoneTracker] #1 'PhoneCam': listening for pose packets on UDP port 9050`).
+
+## Following the active cinematic camera
+
+**Follow Active Camera** (Transform Mapping, default on) makes the tracker drive whichever
+Cinematic Camera is currently active instead of its own entity — so the phone becomes the
+operator of whatever camera the console command `ccam_slot N` (or a Schematyc `Activate`)
+selected. The active camera entity is resolved through the C entry point
+`CryGetActiveCinematicCameraEntity()` exported by `CinematicCamera.dll`.
+
+On every switch:
+
+- The tracker **re-anchors** on the new camera: its reference transform is re-captured from
+  where that camera was placed, and the next pose re-captures the tracker origin against it
+  (the recenter path), so the phone carries on from wherever the new camera sits instead of
+  teleporting it. The phone's own frame is left alone — no control packet is sent.
+- The pose filter is reset, so no transient from the previous camera carries over.
+- The **lens link follows too**: the new camera's optics are resolved and immediately handed
+  the lens state the phone last sent, so the cut does not land on stale lens values.
+- The switch is logged: `[PhoneTracker] #1 'PhoneCam': controller now drives 'CamB'`.
+
+When no cinematic camera is active (or the CinematicCamera plugin is not loaded), the tracker
+falls back to driving its own entity.
+
+## Coordinates and Transform Mapping
+
+ARCore and CRYENGINE are both right handed, so only an axis swap is needed: position
+`(x, y, z)` -> `(x, -z, y)`, quaternion `(qx, qy, qz, qw)` -> `(qx, -qz, qy, qw)` (matching
+`tools/pose_monitor.py`).
+
+Pose pipeline order: **PoseFilter (tracker space, metres) -> MapToWorld (origin / yaw / scale /
+offset) -> optional legacy smoothing -> written to the entity**. All thresholds operate in
+physical units and are unaffected by `Metres To Units`.
+
+**Align Yaw On Start** (default on): anchoring uses only the yaw of the starting poses (phone
+and entity alike); pitch and roll stay gravity aligned, so turning the phone always rotates the
+entity around the world up axis. With it off, a phone tilted at capture time tilts the whole
+rotation frame. With the phone looking straight up or down the heading is taken from the up
+axis instead, so it never degenerates.
+
+Recenter (the Schematyc function, or the phone recentering itself — the incrementing
+`originEpoch` is followed automatically) takes the **filtered** pose as the new origin (so
+jitter is never frozen into it) and re-captures the current target transform as the reference,
+so recentering never teleports the entity.
+
+## PoseFilter pipeline
+
+`Module/PoseFilter.h`, header-only, no `gEnv`, no dynamic allocation, unit-testable outside the
+engine. Four stages:
+
+| Stage | Runs | Contents |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| A clock rebasing | per packet | Maps phone frame timestamps onto the engine clock: an EMA absorbs drift (at most 2 ms correction per packet); a deviation over 200 ms is treated as a phone clock jump and resets the set. |
+| B One Euro | per packet | Position uses one cutoff for all three axes (`posMinCutoff + posBeta * speed`); rotation takes the shortest arc with an angular-rate adaptive cutoff. |
+| B' fixed delay resampling | per render frame | 16-slot ring buffer sampled `packet interval * Resample Delay` behind the engine clock: cubic Hermite for position (tangents from the filtered velocity), slerp for rotation. During a signal gap the pose is extrapolated for at most `Max Extrapolation` ms (velocity decaying linearly), then frozen on the last pose — never snapping back. |
+| C virtual tripod | per render frame | See below; Cinematic mode only. |
+
+### Pose Filter properties
+
+| Property | Range | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Filter Mode | Off / One Euro / Cinematic | Cinematic | Off reproduces the unfiltered path exactly; One Euro = stages A+B+B'; Cinematic adds the virtual tripod. |
+| Position Min Cutoff | 0-10 Hz (slider 0-5) | 1.0 | Lower values kill more jitter while the camera is still. |
+| Position Speed Coefficient | 0-5 per m/s (slider 0-2) | 0.5 | How fast the position cutoff opens up with speed. Raise it if fast moves feel laggy. |
+| Rotation Min Cutoff | 0-10 Hz (slider 0-5) | 1.2 | Rotational jitter suppression while still. |
+| Rotation Speed Coefficient | 0-5 per rad/s (slider 0-2) | 0.1 | How fast the rotation cutoff opens up with angular rate. |
+| Resample Delay | 1-4 | 1.5 | Packet intervals of buffering used to hide network jitter. Higher is smoother but adds latency. |
+| Max Extrapolation | 0-80 ms | 0 | Milliseconds the pose may be extrapolated into a signal gap. 0 freezes on the last pose. |
+
+## Virtual Tripod
+
+Once the operator holds still the pose locks completely, so composing a shot is rock steady.
+State machine: **Moving -> Arming -> (after Hold Time of stillness) Steady -> (movement)
+Blending -> Moving**.
+
+- Entry: speed below `Tripod Enter Speed` and angular rate below 0.8 deg/s (fixed constant).
+- While Steady the anchor tracks ARCore's long-term drift at 0.1 Hz, but stays **bit-exact**
+  inside a 0.5 mm / 0.02 degree dead band — a phone on a table really does hold the transform
+  perfectly still.
+- Release: further than `Tripod Release Distance` from the anchor, or more than 0.5 degrees of
+  rotation, or faster than 0.05 m/s (the latter two are fixed constants). Release blends back
+  to the live pose over `Tripod Release Blend` seconds with a smoothstep; going still again
+  mid-blend re-locks in place with no visible jump.
+
+| Property | Range | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Virtual Tripod | bool | true | Master switch (Cinematic mode only). |
+| Tripod Enter Speed | 0-1 m/s | 0.015 | Metres per second below which the tripod starts arming. |
+| Tripod Hold Time | 0-2 s (slider 0-1) | 0.25 | Seconds of stillness required before the pose locks. |
+| Tripod Release Distance | 0-1 m | 0.01 | Metres of movement away from the locked pose that releases the tripod. |
+| Tripod Release Blend | 0-2 s (slider 0-1) | 0.15 | Seconds spent blending from the locked pose back to the live pose. |
+
+## Other properties
+
+### Connection
+
+| Property | Range | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Enabled | bool | true | Open the socket and drive the entity while in game/simulation mode. |
+| Listen Port | 1-65535 (slider 1024-65535) | 9050 | UDP port the phone sends pose packets to. |
+| Tracker ID | 0-99 | 0 | Number shown in logs and the debug overlay so multiple trackers can be told apart. 0 = automatic (order of creation). |
+
+### Transform Mapping
+
+| Property | Range | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Follow Active Camera | bool | true | Drive whichever Cinematic Camera is currently active (switch with `ccam_slot N`) instead of this entity. Each switch re-anchors at the new camera's position, so the phone carries on from wherever that camera was placed. Falls back to this entity when no cinematic camera is active. |
+| Apply Position | bool | true | Write the tracked translation into the target transform. |
+| Apply Rotation | bool | true | Write the tracked rotation into the target transform. |
+| Relative To Start | bool | true | Treat the tracker origin as the target transform captured when tracking started. Disable to place the target at raw tracker coordinates. |
+| Align Yaw On Start | bool | true | Anchor using only the yaw of the starting poses; see above. |
+| Metres To Units | 0-1000 (slider 0-10) | 1.0 | Multiplier applied to the tracked translation (1 = 1 metre per engine unit). |
+| Yaw Offset | -360 to 360 deg | 0 | Rotation around Z applied to the tracked motion, to align the phone heading with the scene. |
+| Position Offset | Vec3 | (0, 0, 0) | Extra world space offset added after the tracked translation. |
+
+### Cinematic Lens Link
+
+| Property | Range | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Drive Cinematic Camera | bool | true | Forward the focal length / aperture / focus distance / EV / ISO sent by the phone to the Cinematic Camera component on the driven entity. |
+| Lens Arms DOF And Exposure | bool | true | Let the phone switch depth of field and exposure control on when it starts sending lens values. |
+
+The link does **not** link against CinematicCamera: it resolves the exported C entry point
+`CinematicCamera.dll : CryGetCinematicCameraOptics(IEntity*) -> ICinematicCameraOptics*` at
+runtime (declared in
+`Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/Interface/ICinematicCameraOptics.h`). When the project does
+not load CinematicCamera the result is simply nullptr plus a warning, and the tracker still
+drives the entity on its own.
+
+### Legacy And Debug
+
+| Property | Range | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Smoothing Half Life | 0-5 s (slider 0-1) | 0 | Superseded by the Pose Filter; leave at 0. Above 0 it adds one more exponential smoothing pass after the filter pipeline. |
+| Signal Timeout | 0-60 s (slider 0-10) | 2 | Seconds without a valid pose before tracking is considered lost (the filter is reset on recovery). |
+| Debug Draw | bool | false | Draw connection and pose statistics on screen. |
+
+## Autofocus (AF)
+
+Pressing **AF** on the phone sends a lens packet with the `AutofocusRequest` flag. On the PC
+side a ray is cast along the camera axis from 0.3 m in front of the driven entity out to
+500 m (static / terrain / rigid); the hit distance becomes the focus distance, and with no hit
+the focus racks to infinity (10000 m). The DOF user params are eased by the renderer itself
+(~0.3 s time constant), so the rack glides like a real AF drive. The result is reported back
+with a `SetFocus` control packet (param = distance in millimetres) so the phone's focus fader
+follows and the later 4 Hz lens resends carry it.
+
+## Debug overlay (Debug Draw)
+
+One block per tracker, stacked by creation order so several overlays never overlap.
+
+- Line 1: `Tracker #N 'entity' :port  from IP  -> 'target'  TRACKING/NO SIGNAL  packets N
+  loss %  state N  battery %  app N fps`. `#N` is the Tracker ID, `'entity'` the component's
+  own entity, `IP` the sender address of the last packet (`no phone yet` before the first
+  one), and `'target'` the entity currently driven — the active cinematic camera when
+  following.
+- When the socket is closed the line collapses to `Tracker #N 'entity' :port  <problem>`,
+  where the problem is the port conflict message, `SOCKET CLOSED`, or `DISABLED`.
+- Line 2: the position currently written, `pos (x, y, z)`.
+- Line 3 (filtering enabled): filter mode, tripod state (MOVING / ARMING / STEADY / BLEND) and
+  blend %, speed m/s, angular rate deg/s, effective cutoffs (pos/rot Hz), buffer depth,
+  resample delay ms, and an `EXTRAPOLATING` marker.
+- Line 4 (once a lens packet has arrived): focal mm, f-number, focus m, EV, ISO, plus a
+  `(no Cinematic Camera)` note when no optics could be resolved.
+
+## Protocol (`Module/PhoneTrackerProtocol.h`)
+
+Matches the phone's `net/PacketCodec.kt` and the verification tool `tools/pose_monitor.py`;
+everything little endian over the same UDP socket, `version = 1`.
+
+| Packet | Direction | Size | Magic |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Pose | phone -> PC | 64 bytes | `0x54443350` ('P3DT') |
+| Lens | phone -> PC | 32 bytes | `0x534E4C50` ('PLNS') |
+| Control | PC -> phone | 28 bytes | `0x54433350` ('P3CT') |
+
+**Pose (64B)**: magic, version, flags, seq, originEpoch, deviceNs, frameNs, position px/py/pz
+(ARCore right handed, Y up, metres), quaternion qx/qy/qz/qw, trackingState, failureReason,
+batteryPct, appFps. Flags: `Valid=1` (ARCore TRACKING), `SessionResumed=2`, `OriginMark=4`
+(the phone recentered), `Heartbeat=8`.
+
+**Lens (32B)**: magic, version, flags, seq, focalLengthMm, apertureFNumber, focusDistanceM,
+evCompensation, **iso** (uint32; 0 = an older phone app that does not send it, in which case
+the engine ISO is left alone). Sent immediately when a fader moves, plus a 4 Hz resend, so a
+lost datagram never leaves the engine stuck on an old value. Flags: `EnableDepthOfField=1`,
+`EnableExposure=2`, `AutofocusRequest=4` (one shot).
+
+**Control (28B)**: magic, version, cmd, seq, pcNs, param, reserved. Commands:
+
+| cmd | Name | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 / 2 | Ping / Pong | Keep-alive. |
+| 3 | Recenter | Ask the phone to reset its origin. |
+| 4 | SetRate | Set the send rate. |
+| 5 / 6 | Pause / Resume | Pause / resume. |
+| 7 | SetFocus | PC -> phone: autofocus result, param = focus distance in millimetres. |
+
+## Phone app (androidtracker)
+
+Main screen: connection status card (host:port, transport, pose, seq, rate cap) + **Settings**
+(PC IP, pose port, send rate cap with 0 = native, UDP/TCP) + a **Lens** panel toggle +
+**RECENTER**.
+
+Lens panel:
+
+| Control | Range | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Focal Length | 12-200 mm slider | The engine may quantise it further per Focal Step Mode. |
+| Aperture | f/1 - f/22 slider | |
+| Focus | 0.1-100 m (logarithmic) + an infinity detent at the top | Like a real focus ring: fine up close, coarse far away; at the top = infinity (10000 m). |
+| ISO | 100/200/400/800/1600/3200/6400/12800/25600 | Snaps to the standard sensitivities; the engine maps it onto the noise curve that drives film grain. |
+| EV | -3 to +3, seven buttons | EV compensation. |
+| DOF / Exposure | two switches | Arm the engine-side depth of field / exposure control (needs Lens Arms DOF And Exposure). |
+| AF | button | Trigger the engine-side centre autofocus; the result is written back to the focus slider. |
+| Reset | button | Return every lens value to its default. |
+
+## Schematyc functions
+
+* `Recenter` — use the next pose as the new origin and send a Recenter control packet asking
+  the phone to reset too.
+* `SetTrackingEnabled` — open or close the tracker socket at runtime.
+* `IsTracking` — true while valid poses keep arriving.
+
+## Build and deployment
+
+Both plugins hang off the engine's `Code/CryPlugins/CMakeLists.txt`. The bundled CMake is
+mandatory (a system CMake 4.x fails outright on `CMP0040 OLD` in `InitialSetup.cmake`):
+
+```
+Tools\CMake\Win32\bin\cmake.exe -S . -B solutions_cmake\win64
+Tools\CMake\Win32\bin\cmake.exe --build solutions_cmake\win64 --config Profile --target CryPhoneTracker
+Tools\CMake\Win32\bin\cmake.exe --build solutions_cmake\win64 --config Profile --target CinematicCamera
+```
+
+Deployment: copy the DLLs from `bin\win_x64\` to the engine directory actually being run
+(`cryengine-57-lts\5.7.1\bin\win_x64\`) and to the gamesdk-sample-project2 project's `bin\`
+directory; deploy the modified shaders as loose files to the engine's
+`engine\shaders\HWScripts\CryFX\`.
+
+## Enabling
+
+Add to the `.cryproject` plugin list:
+
+```json
+{ "guid": "", "type": "EType::Native", "path": "CryPhoneTracker" },
+```
+
+(`cryengine-gamesdk-sample-project2\5.7.1\gamesdk.cryproject` already has it; the original is
+backed up as `gamesdk.cryproject.pretracker.backup`.)
+
+## Usage
+
+1. Pick an entity -> Add Component -> **Cameras / Cinematic Camera**, then Add Component ->
+   **Tracking / Phone Tracker**.
+2. In the phone app enter the PC's LAN IP and a port matching `Listen Port` (default 9050),
+   transport UDP.
+3. Enter Game Mode (Ctrl+G) or Simulation; the component opens the socket and starts updating
+   the entity.
+4. Press **Lens** on the phone to open the fader panel; press **RECENTER** to reset the origin.
+5. Turn on `Debug Draw` to watch the connection and filter state.
+6. With **Follow Active Camera** on, place several Cinematic Cameras, give each one a Camera
+   Slot, and cut between them with `ccam_slot N` (bind it to the number keys) — the phone takes
+   over whichever camera is active.
